&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Caylent is an AI-first cloud services company that helps organizations turn ambitious ideas into meaningful business impact. As an AWS Premier Tier Services Partner and a charter member of Anthropic’s Claude Partner Network, we combine deep expertise in AWS, artificial intelligence, and Anthropic’s Claude platform to help customers modernize their technology, build intelligent products, and move AI from experimentation into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our capabilities span generative and agentic AI, cloud migration and modernization, cloud-native application development, data and analytics, DevOps, managed services, security and compliance, and customer experience transformation. At Caylent, our people always come first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a fully remote global company with employees in Canada, the United States and Latin America. We celebrate the culture of each of our team members and foster a community of technological curiosity. Come talk to us to learn more about what it means to be a Caylien!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a skilled Web Automation Test Engineer to join our growing Quality Assurance and Testing&amp;nbsp;practice. The right candidate is someone who has hands-on expertise building scalable test automation&amp;nbsp;frameworks, with a strong emphasis on reliability, maintainability, and rapid feedback for CI/CD pipelines. Your&amp;nbsp;mission will be to design, develop, and maintain robust web automation frameworks for API and functional testing,&amp;nbsp;enabling our teams to deliver high-quality cloud-native solutions. You&#39;ll work with modern tools like Playwright&amp;nbsp;and collaborate closely with developers and QA teams to drive automation best practices across our projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Your Assignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain a scalable web automation framework for API and UI/functional testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop test strategies, test plans, and automation suites using Playwright (Python/TypeScript) for web&amp;nbsp;applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reusable, modular page objects and components to maximize test reuse and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement API testing strategies (REST/GraphQL) integrated with UI tests where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear, maintainable automated tests with robust assertions and meaningful reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate tests with CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Jenkins, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure test data management, environment handling, and test environment provisioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement parallel test execution, flaky test handling, retry strategies, and test isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor test results, analyze failures, and provide timely root-cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with developers, QA, and product teams to ensure quality goals are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document framework usage, coding standards, and create comprehensive onboarding guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with automation tooling trends and propose improvements to testing infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Your Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on experience in web automation testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Playwright (Python/TypeScript) for end-to-end web testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building automation frameworks from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Python/TypeScript with good knowledge of software design patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with API testing (REST/GraphQL) and integrating API tests with UI tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with test frameworks (pytest, unittest)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of CI/CD integration and test reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with version control (Git) and collaborative workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Xray Test Management for Jira for integrating test plans/results with Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavior-Driven Development (BDD) experience and tooling (e.g., Gherkin, Cucumber, Behave)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of performance testing fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docker and containerized test environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud-based test environments and device/browser farms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with test data management and data-driven testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to Agile/Scrum development processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
